Schur elements and the a-function
The canonical symmetrising form τ on H(W) (see Assumptions 3.4) can be extended to K(v)H(W) by
extension of scalars, and can be used to deﬁne Schur elements (sE)E∈Irr(W ) for H(W), as in the real
case. The Schur elements of H(W) have been explicitly calculated for all complex reﬂection groups:
• for ﬁnite Coxeter groups see §2.2;
• for complex reﬂection groups of type G(l, 1, n) by Geck–Iancu–Malle [GIM] and Mathas [Mat];
• for complex reﬂection groups of type G(l, 2, 2) by Malle [Mal2];
• for the non-Coxeter exceptional complex reﬂection groups by Malle [Mal2
